ADDITIONAL COMMERCIAL CONDITIONS

1. Definitions.

   "Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
   common control with a licensee.

   "Commercial Payment Use" means production use of the Work to directly
   initiate, orchestrate, route, attribute, recover, or confirm payment
   transactions for a licensee or its customers.

   "Successful Payment Transaction" means a production transaction for which
   a payment service returns a final successful status. Failed, cancelled,
   test, sandbox, and duplicate callback events are excluded.

   "Cumulative Payment Volume" means the aggregate gross US-dollar value of
   all Successful Payment Transactions processed through Commercial Payment
   Use by a licensee and all of its Affiliates from their first production use
   of the Work. It does not reset. Refunds, reversals, and chargebacks do not
   reduce the amount already counted.

   "Commercial License" means a separate written agreement signed by the
   applicable copyright holder or its authorized licensing representative.

2. Free Commercial Tier.

   Subject to this license, Commercial Payment Use is permitted without a
   separate Commercial License while Cumulative Payment Volume does not exceed
   USD 1,000,000 (one million United States dollars).

3. Commercial License Required Above the Threshold.

   Before processing any Successful Payment Transaction that would cause
   Cumulative Payment Volume to exceed USD 1,000,000, the licensee must obtain
   a Commercial License. Fees, payment terms, support, and any additional
   rights are governed by that Commercial License.

   The threshold is aggregated across the licensee and all Affiliates and may
   not be reset or multiplied by separating deployments, accounts, API keys,
   products, currencies, transaction identifiers, or legal entities.

4. Measurement and Verification.

   Non-USD transactions are converted using the exchange rate shown on the
   applicable payment-service settlement statement. The licensee must retain
   reasonably sufficient aggregate records to prevent duplicate counting and
   verify Cumulative Payment Volume. Those records need not contain payer
   identities, payment credentials, complete order contents, or other personal
   information unnecessary for verification.

   When there is a reasonable basis to believe the free tier has been
   exceeded, the copyright holder may request, no more than once in any
   twelve-month period, a written statement of Cumulative Payment Volume.

5. Prohibited Circumvention.

   A licensee may not intentionally evade, remove, or falsify measurement or
   currency-conversion logic used to apply these conditions, or structure its
   use to evade the threshold described above.

6. Other Uses.

   These Additional Commercial Conditions impose no fee or payment-volume
   threshold on uses that are not Commercial Payment Use. Such uses remain
   governed by the Apache License reproduced below.

7. Cure and Termination.

   If a licensee breaches Sections 2 through 5 and does not cure the breach
   within thirty days after written notice, the rights granted under this
   combined license terminate for that licensee. Intentional circumvention may
   be terminated immediately by written notice. Reinstatement requires a
   written agreement from the applicable copyright holder. Termination does
   not extinguish payment obligations accrued before termination.

8. Prior Releases.

   Releases previously distributed under GNU General Public License version 3
   remain available under that license. These terms do not retroactively revoke
   rights already granted for those releases.

9. Relationship to the Apache License.

   For Commercial Payment Use, these Additional Commercial Conditions are
   additional conditions of the copyright license and control in the event of
   a conflict. Otherwise, the Apache License controls. Because of these added
   conditions, this combined license is not the unmodified Apache License 2.0
   and should not be identified solely by the SPDX expression "Apache-2.0".

